                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 1 — Find which mailbox sends mail for the country</h4>
                <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">Typical convention (already deployed):</p>
                <ul style="margin:0 0 12px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li><code style="background:#1e293b;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;">sales@tertiarycourses.com.ng</code> — Nigeria</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="margin:0 0 4px;color:#94a3b8;font-size:12px;">Verify the mailbox exists in <a href="https://admin.google.com/ac/users" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;">Google Workspace Admin → Directory → Users</a>.</p>

                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 2 — Sign in as that mailbox (NOT as admin)</h4>
                <p style="margin:0 0 6px;">Open an <strong>incognito window</strong> → <a href="https://accounts.google.com" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;">accounts.google.com</a> → sign in as the country mailbox (e.g. <code style="background:#1e293b;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;">sales@tertiarycourses.com.ng</code>).</p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 4px;color:#94a3b8;font-size:12px;">If you don't know the password, from the Workspace admin console click <strong>Reset Password</strong> on that user, set a temporary one, then use it.</p>

                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 3 — Confirm 2-Step Verification is ON</h4>
                <p style="margin:0 0 6px;">Go to <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/security" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;">myaccount.google.com/security</a> → check the "2-Step Verification" tile. If it says "Off", click it and walk through the setup (SMS or Authenticator app). App Passwords don't exist without 2SV on.</p>

                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 4 — Generate the App Password</h4>
                <p style="margin:0 0 6px;">Open <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;"><strong>myaccount.google.com/apppasswords</strong></a> (this URL only works after 2SV is on; there's no sidebar link).</p>
                <ol style="margin:0 0 6px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li>App name: <code style="background:#1e293b;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;">MMS Nigeria SMTP</code></li>
                    <li>Click <strong>Create</strong></li>
                    <li>Google shows a <strong>16-character password</strong> like <code style="background:#1e293b;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;">abcd efgh ijkl mnop</code></li>
                    <li><strong style="color:#fbbf24;">Copy it immediately</strong> — Google won't show it again; you'd have to generate a new one.</li>
                </ol>

                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 5 — Paste into the country's card below</h4>
                <ol style="margin:0 0 6px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li>Click the <strong>Gmail / Workspace</strong> quick-fill button → Host / Port / SSL / Auth fill themselves</li>
                    <li><strong>Username</strong>: the country mailbox (e.g. <code style="background:#1e293b;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:3px;font-size:12px;">sales@tertiarycourses.com.ng</code>)</li>
                    <li><strong>Password</strong>: paste the 16-char App Password (spaces ok, Google strips them)</li>
                    <li>Click <strong>Save Credentials</strong> at the bottom of the page — status pill flips to <span style="color:#34d399;font-weight:600;">Active</span></li>
                </ol>

                <h4 style="margin:18px 0 8px;color:#f1f5f9;font-size:13px;">Step 6 — Verify with Send Test</h4>
                <p style="margin:0 0 6px;">In the card's "test recipient" field enter your own email → click <strong>Send Test</strong>. Within a few seconds the inline result shows either:</p>
                <ul style="margin:0 0 6px 18px;padding:0;">
                    <li><span style="color:#34d399;font-weight:600;">Accepted by smtp.gmail.com:587</span> → check your inbox, the test mail will be there</li>
                    <li><span style="color:#fecaca;font-weight:600;">"Username and Password not accepted"</span> → wrong App Password (typo when pasting, or you copied the masked dots). Re-generate from <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords" target="_blank" style="color:#60a5fa;">myaccount.google.com/apppasswords</a>.</li>
                    <li><span style="color:#fecaca;font-weight:600;">Connection timed out</span> → wrong host (you're not on Gmail). Use a different preset or your provider's real SMTP host.</li>
                </ul>

